# bcrypt/tests: Avoid crash when BCryptSecretAgreement fails in test_ECDH_alg.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11088 state=closed
# The test pattern page shows a bcrypt crash. I could reproduce it with a Debian Bookworm VM.

It shows before the crash the error:
```
GnuTLS error: An unknown public key algorithm was encountered.
bcrypt.c:3332: Test failed: L"ECDH_P256": got 0xc00000e5
```

The crashes can be avoid by initializing the handles `secret` and `key2` to NULL.

[Test pattern page bcrypt:bcrypt](https://test.winehq.org/data/patterns.html#bcrypt:bcrypt)

[Testbot run with this patch](https://testbot.winehq.org/JobDetails.pl?Key=163281)

